# =============================================================================
# Mirage native patch 0002 — canvas serialization noise
# Target tag: 131.0.6778.85 (verify every anchor against this checkout)
# =============================================================================
#
# WHAT
#   toDataURL / toBlob / OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob serialization noise.
#   The JS layer (inject/canvas.js) noises the direct pixel readout
#   (getImageData) but deliberately cannot touch serialization: editing the
#   produced data-URL string breaks its validity, and decode+re-encode from
#   JS is async, slow and detectable by timing (inject/README.md, wave-1 gap).
#
#   This patch applies the SAME deterministic per-pixel noise at the input of
#   the platform image encoders: for pixel (x, y) flip the LSB of channel
#   MirageInt(seed, x, y, 4) when MirageNoise(seed, x, y) < 0.03 — a bit-exact
#   C++ port of inject/rng.js + inject/canvas.js, keyed on (canvasSeed, x, y)
#   in absolute canvas coordinates. Consequences:
#     - a PNG decoded from toDataURL matches a getImageData(0, 0, w, h) read
#       of the same canvas (the "same noised pixel path" required by
#       inject/README.md — no read-path divergence for a detector to see);
#     - the PNG stays perfectly valid: noise is applied to pixels BEFORE
#       encoding, not to encoded bytes;
#     - worker contexts (OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob inside a Worker) are
#       covered — the JS inject layer never runs in workers;
#     - stable per profile, different across profiles, invisible to the eye.
#
#   getImageData itself is NOT touched here (JS layer owns the read path).
#
# WHERE (two encoder entry paths, blocks 1-3 and 4-6):
#   A. third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/image_data_buffer.cc
#      — synchronous encode path behind HTMLCanvasElement.toDataURL.
#        Search signals:
#          grep -n "ImageDataBuffer::ToDataURL\|ImageDataBufferBase::ToDataURL" third_party/blink/renderer/platform/graphics/image_data_buffer.cc
#          grep -rn "ImageDataBuffer::Create" third_party/blink/renderer/modules/canvas/canvas2d/html_canvas_element.cc
#   B. third_party/blink/renderer/modules/canvas/canvas2d/canvas_async_blob_creator.cc
#      — async progressive encode behind toBlob / convertToBlob.
#        Search signal:
#          grep -rn "class CanvasAsyncBlobCreator" third_party/blink/renderer/modules/canvas/
#   If either file moved in the tag, locate it with the search signals above
#   and re-pin MIRAGE-FILE.
#
# ODR NOTE
#   Blocks 2 and 5 insert an identical `namespace mirage` helper set into two
#   translation units. All helpers are `inline`, so the ODR-identical
#   definitions merge at link time (function-local statics are shared — the
#   config is read once per process). Keep the two copies byte-identical
#   when editing.

